                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Second conditional",
                    "explanation": "El segundo condicional habla de situaciones imaginarias o poco probables, en el presente o en el futuro: If + past simple, would + verbo. If I went, I'd have to leave the pub.\n\nAunque el verbo está en pasado, no hablamos del pasado: «si fuera», «si tuviera».\n\nPara dar consejos: If I were you, I'd… (were sirve para todas las personas).\n\nCompáralo con el primer condicional, que habla de algo posible y real: If you promise to visit me, I'll go.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "",
                        "Estructura",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "1.er condicional (posible)",
                          "If + presente, will",
                          "If you promise to visit me, I'll go."
                        ],
                        [
                          "2.º condicional (imaginario)",
                          "If + pasado, would",
                          "If I went, I'd have to leave the pub."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Consejo",
                          "If I were you, I'd…",
                          "If I were you, I'd go."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "What would you do if…?",
                          "What would you do if it didn't work?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "wouldn't",
                          "If you left, I wouldn't be happy."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "If I were you, I'd go. It's your dream.",
                      "What would I do if it didn't work?",
                      "If it didn't work, you'd come back.",
                      "If you left, the kitchen would be much tidier!"
                    ]
                  }
                },
